    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d192">

                <pb facs="0296" n="180" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg180"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 817.00/2369.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Gonzales.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-12-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 4, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>General Luis Mena, Nicaraguan revolutionist, has been reported at Central Sugar
                    Company, Guantanamo, until November 23. It is stated that General Mena left Cuba
                    for Costa Rica for the purpose of starting revolutionary activity against
                    Government of Nicaragua. Request Cuban Government to furnish you with all
                    information obtainable regarding his movements. Report by telegraph.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
